1. f4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 g6 4. b3 Bg7 5. Bb2 O-O 6. Be2 c5 7. O-O Nc6 8. Ne5 {
alternativt c4 eller Dc1 evt. De1} 8... Bd7 {svart passivt - mer aktivt er d4.}
9. Bf3 {hvit far na et lite overtak} 9... Rc8 10. Nc3 e6 {Atalik: 'Black plays
a Queen's Indian with tempo down.However it is very difficult to say whites
hypermodern setup can make the tempo useful.'} (10... d4 $5 11. exd4 cxd4 12.
Ne2 Nxe5 13. fxe5 Ng4 14. Nxd4 Nxe5 15. Bxb7 Rb8 (15... Nc4 16. Bc3 $1 (16.
bxc4 Rxc4 17. c3 Bxd4+ 18. cxd4 Rb4 19. Ba3 Rxb7 20. Qf3 $11) 16... Ne3 17.
dxe3 Rxc3 18. Qd2 Qc7 19. Be4 Rd8 $44) 16. Be4 Bg4 (16... Nc4 $6 17. bxc4 Rxb2
18. Nb3 $16) 17. Qe1 Nc4 18. bxc4 Bxd4+ (18... Rxb2 19. Nb3) 19. Bxd4 Qxd4+ $11
) 11. Ne2 {Sa langt helt likt et tidligere seniorNM mot Eigil hvor sort spilte
Se8! og det ble remis. Na prover sort en annen variant men med mindre hell.
'!?' Atalik.} (11. d4 {looks more to the point.} 11... Qa5 $5 $13) 11... Ne4 {
'!' Atalik.  Atalik: 'I like this more than Ioardachescu's Ne8.'} 12. Nxc6 Bxc6
13. Bxg7 Kxg7 14. d4 (14. d3 Nd6 15. Qd2 b6 16. Rad1 (16. b4 Bb7 $1 $13 (16...
cxb4 17. Qxb4 Nf5 18. g4 Nh4 19. Bh1 $36)) 16... f5 $1 {
Preparing f6 square for the Q.} 17. d4 $6 (17. c4 Qf6 18. Qc3 $11) 17... c4 $1
{Black takes over the initiative.} 18. b4 a5 19. a3 (19. bxa5 $6 b5 $1 $17)
19... Ra8 20. Ra1 Rf7 21. Rfb1 Rfa7 $6 (21... Ra6 22. Nc3 b5 23. Ra2 Rfa7 24.
Rba1 Qa8 $17) 22. Qc1 axb4 23. axb4 Nb5 24. Rxa7+ Rxa7 25. Ra1 Qa8 26. Rxa7+
Qxa7 27. c3 Qa2 $6 {Another inexactitude.} (27... Qa3 $1 {was natural and good.
} 28. Qe1 $8 (28. Qxa3 $2 Nxa3 29. Kf2 Nb1 30. Ke1 Ba4 $19) 28... Qb2 $11) 28.
g4 Na3 29. Kf2 Nb1 30. gxf5 $2 (30. h4 {
After this move it is blacks turn to be careful.} 30... Nd2 31. gxf5 exf5 32.
Qg1 Qb1 $1 (32... Nxf3 $2 33. Kxf3 h5 (33... Qc2 34. h5 Qe4+ 35. Kf2 Be8 36.
Qg5 $16) 34. Qg5 Kf7 35. Qd8 Qa7 36. Ng1 $16) (32... Ne4+ $2 33. Bxe4 dxe4 34.
Qg5 Ba4 35. Qe7+ Kh6 36. Qa7 $1 $16) 33. Qxb1 (33. Qg2 h5 34. Ng1 Nxf3 $11)
33... Nxb1 34. Ke1 Kf6 35. Kd1 Ke6 36. Kc1 Na3 37. Ng1 Nb5 38. Kd2 Nd6 $11)
30... exf5 31. h4 (31. b5 Ba8 32. h4 h5 {transposes}) 31... h5 $1 32. Qg1 $6 {
It is very strange that some sharp tactician like Pavel is reluctant to insert
b5 in this position.} (32. b5 Ba8 33. Qg1 Nxc3 34. Bxh5 Ne4+ 35. Kf3 Nd2+ $11)
32... Nxc3 33. Qg5 $1 (33. Bxh5 $2 Be8 34. Bf3 (34. Bxg6 $4 Qxe2+) 34... Qd2
35. h5 Nd1+ 36. Kg3 Nxe3 $19) 33... Be8 $4 {The double question mark goes to
tactical inability to see simple exchange of queens from my part.Objectively
due to impregnance of whites camp still after the missed oppurtunity the
bishops endgame is a draw.} (33... Qxe2+ 34. Bxe2 Ne4+ 35. Ke1 Nxg5 36. fxg5
Kf7 $1 (36... Ba4 37. Bf3 $11) (36... c3 37. b5 Bd7 38. Bd3 f4 39. exf4 Bg4 40.
Kf2 Bd1 41. Ke3 $11) (36... f4 37. exf4 $11) 37. Bd1 Ke6 (37... Bd7 38. Bc2 Ke6
39. Kd2 $11) (37... c3 38. Bb3 Ke6 39. Kd1 Bb5 40. Kc2 Bc4 41. Bxc4 dxc4 42. b5
$11) 38. Kd2 $1 $11 (38. Bc2 $4 c3 39. Kd1 Bb5 40. Kc1 Be2 $19)) 34. Qe7+ Bf7
35. Qe5+ Kg8 36. Qb8+ Kg7 37. Qe5+ {
1/2-1/2 Blatny,P-Atalik,S/Stratton Mountain 2000/CBM 78/[Atalik] (37)}) 14...
b6 15. Bxe4 {hvit oker sin fordel} 15... dxe4 16. c4 Qe7 17. Qc2 Rfd8 18. Rad1
Rc7 19. Qc3 f6 20. dxc5 Rxd1 21. Rxd1 Qxc5 22. a4 Kf7 23. Nd4 a6 {
avgjorende feiltrekk - bedre er Ld7 selv om hvit fortsatt star bedre.} 24. Nxc6
Qxc6 25. Qd4 b5 {svakt trekk men andre trekk nytter heller ikke} 26. cxb5 axb5
27. a5 h5 28. h3 {Sort ga her opp - noe vel tidlig? Men sort er kommet i en
vanskelig defensiv posisjon og fribonden pa a5 vil avgjore til slutt. Og som
Eigil sjol sier i en sluttkommentar: slike stillinger er de verste jeg vet.
Noe vel de aller fleste vil vare enig med ham i. Der kunne fulgt: 28.- Kg7 29.
Kh2 Tf7 30.Db4 med stor fordel for hvit} 1-0

